      "id": "A1",
      "statement": "Two hypothetical identified recorded objects; neither is asserted to meet the entire Artifact Definition."
    },
    {
      "basis": "Authority normative statement and formal expression; root legitimacy is an external premise.",
      "id": "A2",
      "statement": "The finite grant templates represent possible owner-qualified roots for scope:pilot-local-use. Each model independently selects whether an owner act occurred, materializes the matching claim and active grant together, and checks matching fields. Root legitimacy is assumed, not established from record presence. No active grant exists for the provenance-only witness."
    },
    {
      "basis": "Provenance formal expression. The empty sequence allowed by star is not modeled as an inhabited recorded trail.",
      "id": "A3",
      "statement": "Recorded provenance is a nonempty typed path; missing segments require explicit residue and an owner route. Unrecorded means unavailable to this model, not no historical origin."
    },
    {
      "basis": "Provenance applicability: use before promoting; stronger per-instance policy is candidate and owner review pending.",
      "id": "A4",
      "statement": "In this admission-use profile, authority requires recorded provenance. This is an explicit selected workflow coupling, not global Authority implies Provenance."
    },
    {
      "basis": "Governance invariant formal expression and no-silent-substitution boundary.",
      "id": "A5",
      "statement": "A move changes only intended or explicitly recorded axes. Recording a coupling does not itself create an authority root."
    },
    {
      "basis": "Selected finite profile only.",
      "id": "A6",
      "statement": "Search covers 192 configurations: 8 per-object choices squared times 3 move choices, with fixed strings, root set and scope."
    }
  ],
